# Test-plan case hcert-contract-maintenance (test/plans/hcert-library-conformance.test-plan.json).
# One Scenario per executable test; the @test: tag names the test that runs it.
@case:hcert-contract-maintenance
Feature: Keep the contract and everything generated from it current
  The WIT, its TypeScript view and Kotlin skeleton, the CDDL, and the payload
  models derived from the FHIR logical models.

  @req:stt-gen-010
  @test:tools/hcert-rust/tests/architecture.rs::stt_gen_010_the_component_exports_the_wit_contract
  Scenario: The component exports the WIT contract (Rust)
    Given tools/hcert-rust/src/component.rs
    Then its bindings are generated from path "../../api/wit"
    And they are for world "hcert"
    And api/wit/worlds.wit declares "world hcert"

  @req:stt-gen-014 @req:stt-gen-010
  @test:tools/hcert-kotlin/hcert-core/src/jvmTest/kotlin/who/smart/trust/core/ArchitectureTest.kt::ArchitectureTest::STT-GEN-014_STT-GEN-010_the_API_is_generated_from_the_contract_and_names_no_WIT
  Scenario: The API is generated from the contract and names no WIT (Kotlin)
    Given the files of tools/hcert-kotlin/hcert-api/src/commonMain, at least one
    Then each starts with "// GENERATED by tools/wit2kotlin/wit2kotlin.py"
    And after that first line none names "WIT", "World" or "WitResult"
